      contexto: 'Mevir - Dr. Alberto Gallinal Heber is a non-state public entity created by article 473 of law 13.640, of 26 December 1967, to eradicate substandard rural housing; it took its current name under law 18.676 of 2010. It builds homes, productive buildings, community services and infrastructure (water, electricity, sanitation) in rural areas and small towns, with labour contributed by the participants themselves, and finances the houses with instalments of up to 25 years that recipients repay, with part subsidised. It works with rural wage earners and low-income small family farmers.',
      hallazgo: 'The national internal audit office (AIN) assessed the Nucleated Housing and Urban Plot programmes — participant selection, purchasing of materials and supplies, and post-construction follow-up — covering programmes delivered between 2016 and 2020, and signed its report on 23 March 2022. It rated three findings as "extreme" risk: the concentration of functions in the Social Management department, the participant selection and contracting process, and post-construction follow-up together with arrears. Three more were rated "high": materials purchasing and inventory; the hierarchical structure of its units — which includes the absence of an Internal Audit Unit, mandatory under article 239 of law 19.924; and strategic decision-making. The report concluded that management showed internal control weaknesses that do not allow transparency to be assured in the selection of participants or in the setting of the instalments and subsidies granted, matching what Telenoche published. On arrears, out of a sample of 189 active accounts, 32.80% were more than six instalments behind and 26.45% more than twelve — some 3,164,960 pesos in the latter case — and 8% of the total were more than 25 instalments behind.',
