      porQueImporta: 'Mevir builds homes for rural families with no other option and then charges them instalments. If there is no way to assure how it is decided who gets in and who is left out, nor to collect what was lent, the money that should come back to build the next batch of homes does not come back.',
      caveat: 'Mevir is a non-state public entity: some of its purchasing is not published through the same channel as ministries\', so what appears in the search engine may be only a portion of what it buys. The audit also did not cover the Rural Area programmes, the agreements, or the refurbishment, sanitation and reallocation schemes.',
