      dek: 'Prosecutors proved more than US$ 1.2 million was siphoned from the fund that finances housing for construction workers; the money was never recovered.',
      contexto: 'The Fondo Social de Vivienda de Obreros de la Construcción (Fosvoc) manages resources earmarked for housing solutions and social programmes for workers in the sector, funded by the sector\'s own contributions rather than by national budget allocations. According to El Observador, the scheme was uncovered when the employee in charge took leave and the worker who replaced her spotted unusual movements in the institution\'s bank accounts. The investigation was assigned to the third-shift Economic and Complex Crimes Prosecutor\'s Office, under prosecutor Gilberto Rodríguez.',
      hallazgo: 'Búsqueda reported that the investigation proved a "criminal ring" and that the amount diverted exceeds US$ 1.2 million. El Observador reported that prosecutors reached an agreement with the employee who carried out 193 irregular transactions worth 35,627,581 pesos and US$ 17,500, and that the prosecutor had already obtained, at an earlier hearing in June, the conviction of three former Sunca union officials. On 15 December 2025 four more people — three men and one woman — were convicted through abbreviated proceedings for repeated counts of misappropriation as co-perpetrators and one count of assisting activities preceding money laundering, according to la diaria; some US$ 400,000 had been deposited into those four convicts\' accounts. They received obligations to keep a fixed address, report weekly to their local police station and perform ten months of community service.',
      statusNote: 'As of this file\'s closing (August 2026), Búsqueda counted eight people convicted after a year of investigation. According to that outlet, the outstanding issue is redress: no restitution was ordered and the Fosvoc\'s lawyer, Óscar López Goldaracena, said "the big shortfall is reparation", so the fund was considering civil actions in 2026 to recover the money. Búsqueda adds that prosecutors still had to pursue hypotheses about the financing of the Sunca union and the Communist Party with diverted money, lines that as of this file\'s closing had not led to any known charges: the investigation remains open.',
      porQueImporta: 'This is money construction workers contribute so they can access a home. Every dollar diverted is a housing solution that was not delivered, and so far the courts have convicted eight people but have not managed to get the money returned to the fund.',
      caveat: 'The Fosvoc is not a State body and is not financed by the national budget: its resources come from the sector\'s own contributions. That is why this case leaves no contracts or payments traceable in the public procurement search engine. The lines of investigation still open are prosecutors\' hypotheses, not proven facts.',
